{
  "failure_mode": "collision",
  "evidence": [
    "run c51t22_s288052211: collision at t=52.1 s with mover_03 while robot speed 0.29 m/s; first detection of mover at t=47.12 s bearing -105° (outside front‑gap angle) and later at bearing -49° still not triggering stop",
    "run c51t22_s1475949886: time limit abort at t=50.5 s (budget exhausted) with robot still 8 m from goal; many stop/turn episodes indicate frequent stopping without progress",
    "pass runs (e.g., c51t22_s76695582) show first_not_on_map at t≈52 s while robot continues at >1 m/s, indicating side movers are not causing stop"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "assumption": "2D lidar reliably detects moving objects within 8 m",
      "holds": true,
      "why": "first_not_on_map timestamps show detections at 2‑5 m in all runs"
    },
    {
      "assumption": "Front‑gap detection (±30°) is sufficient to catch obstacles that can cause collision",
      "holds": false,
      "why": "collision run shows mover at bearing -49° and -33° never entered front‑gap, yet caused collision"
    },
    {
      "assumption": "TTC horizon _TTC_H = 1 s provides enough reaction time for moving objects",
      "holds": false,
      "why": "collision occurred despite mover being visible >5 s earlier; TTC check missed the future intersection"
    },
    {
      "assumption": "Stop distance _STOP_D = 1.5 m and stop‑wait 1 s guarantee safety",
      "holds": false,
      "why": "collision happened when mover was <1 m but not in front‑gap, so stop condition never triggered"
    },
    {
      "assumption": "Reducing _STOP_WAIT to 1 s speeds up runs without harming safety",
      "holds": false,
      "why": "turn 22 shows both a new collision and a time‑limit failure after the reduction"
    }
  ],
  "approach_families": [
    {
      "family": "basic front‑gap stop/detour (no side checks)",
      "turns": "0,1,3,4,8,10,22",
      "result": "turn 8: 9/9 pass (slow); other turns: mixed passes with collisions or stalls"
    },
    {
      "family": "danger‑close side detection",
      "turns": "11,13,21",
      "result": "7/9, 7/10, 7/8 passes – still occasional collisions or timeouts"
    },
    {
      "family": "speed scaling by min mover distance",
      "turns": "15",
      "result": "8/10 passes – collisions reduced but still a timeout"
    },
    {
      "family": "velocity‑obstacle candidate filtering",
      "turns": "6",
      "result": "7/8 passes – collision reduced, but runtime increased"
    },
    {
      "family": "reverse‑state backing away",
      "turns": "19,20,21",
      "result": "7/8 passes – improved safety but added complexity"
    }
  ],
  "candidates": [
    {
      "idea": "Add a proximity‑based stop and speed‑scaling using the minimum distance to any mover (new _min_mover_dist function) and trigger stop when d_min < _STOP_D, combine its scaling with the existing front‑gap factor",
      "new_family": true,
      "for": "captures side movers that are close but outside the ±30° front cone, preventing collisions like in run c51t22_s288052211",
      "risk": "may increase stop frequency and raise total run time, risking the 600 s budget"
    },
    {
      "idea": "Increase TTC horizon _TTC_H to 2 s and raise _SAFE_GO to 0.8 m to give more margin before resuming motion",
      "new_family": false,
      "for": "provides longer prediction window for fast side movers",
      "risk": "could cause excessive stopping, further inflating execution time"
    },
    {
      "idea": "Implement a simple dynamic waypoint offset when a mover is within a safety zone, steering around it without stopping",
      "new_family": false,
      "for": "avoids stopping altogether, keeping average time low",
      "risk": "adds path‑planning complexity and may conflict with static obstacles"
    }
  ],
  "chosen": "Candidate A – add proximity‑based stop and speed scaling, because it directly addresses side‑approaching movers that caused the observed collision while keeping the existing state‑machine structure.",
  "target": "controller logic (add _min_mover_dist, adjust stop condition and speed scaling)",
  "direction": "1. Define constants _PROX_STOP = 1.0 and _PROX_SCALE_MAX = 1.5 near the other safety constants. 2. Add a helper function `_min_mover_dist(pose, movers)` that returns the smallest Euclidean distance from the robot to any mover (or a large value if none). 3. In `controller()`, after `movers = _movers(t, pose)`, compute `d_min = _min_mover_dist(pose, movers)`. 4. Replace the stop trigger `if gap < _STOP_D:` with `if gap < _STOP_D or d_min < _STOP_D:` to also stop for close side movers. 5. Compute a side‑distance scaling factor `f_dist = _clamp((d_min - _PROX_STOP) / _PROX_SCALE_MAX, 0.15, 1.0)` and combine it with the existing front‑gap factor `f` as `scale = min(f, f_dist)`. 6. Apply `scale` to the nominal speed in the candidate loop (`cmd = (v_nom * scale * k, w_nom)`) and in the resume condition, keeping all other state‑machine logic unchanged.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "last_direction_ok": "no – 줄인 정지·우회 대기시간으로 충돌이 새로 발생했고 전체 시뮬 시간도 예산을 초과했습니다.",
  "base_turn": 8
}
